# Spike B report — T-003

Date: 2026-10-17. Owner: spike-b-director. Outcome: **BLOCKED before compilation at milestone 1**.

Would I build the real app on this? **No commitment yet.** This run provides no executable evidence for GPUI/Kit suitability or performance. Registry connectivity must be restored before the mandatory input and editor gates can be judged. This is an environment block, not a framework rejection.

## Build gate and artifacts

- Rust 1.99.1, cargo 1.99.1, host x86_64-pc-windows-msvc; CMake 4.4.4; vswhere matched VS2026 Community with C++ tools at "'`C:'"\\Program Files\\Microsoft Visual Studio\\18\\Community"'`.
- Initial scaffold requested gpui-component =0.7.3 and gpui-pre/platform =0.3.9. Cargo exited 101 in **0.226179 seconds** with inherited CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true and an empty cache. [Log](build.log), [timing](build-result.txt).
- One bounded online retry (process-local offline=false, retry=0, HTTP timeout=20) exited 101 in **6.3128777 seconds**. crates.io index config.json could not be fetched through the configured proxy at 127.0.0.1. [Log](build-online.log), [timing](build-online-result.txt).
- No compilation or linker invocation occurred. VS2026-vs-VS2022 compatibility, Windows SDK completeness, and successful build time are **unknown**. No software installed or global network settings changed.
- After source review, final unbuilt scaffold follows the release hello-window API: gpui-kit =0.7.3 plus an explicit gpui-pre =0.3.9 constraint; default backend, no Fast feature. This final manifest was not retried after the same registry-access failure. No Cargo.lock exists; generating and retaining it is a resume requirement.
- `spikes/B/build.ps1` provides a repeatable build using workspace-local Cargo cache/target paths. `src/main.rs` is a hello-window scaffold only, with no editor or gesture instrumentation.

