## Source review and remaining risks

Read-only Luna high worker reviewed primary release sources; director verified the release manifest and hello example. [v0.7.3 manifest](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/longbridge/gpui-kit/v0.7.3/Cargo.toml) pins GPUI snapshot 0.3.9 and leaves Fast optional. [Release hello source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/longbridge/gpui-kit/v0.7.3/examples/hello_world/src/main.rs) supplies the final scaffold entry points. [Installation guide](https://gpui-kit.com/docs/installation/) documents VS2022, MSVC and CMake; VS2026 success is not established here.

Worker review of the [release editor guide](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/longbridge/gpui-kit/v0.7.3/website/component/editor.md) found EditorState language/line-number/folding options, but paint-only range decorations do not establish interactive inline controls. These remain runtime editor gates.

The existing T-001 report warns that GPUI Ended can follow inertia. This run cannot confirm that behavior against restored 0.3.9 source. If confirmed, the one bounded adapter candidate is to expose RUNNING→INERTIA as a separate release event in the existing Windows Direct Manipulation status callback and READY as completion, retaining native pixel deltas. That is a prospective backend seam, not an implemented or validated fix; zero-motion lift/cancellation paths, DPI and editor arbitration still need proving.

## Measurements, screenshots and effort

Cold launch to editable, hotkey to visible+focused, hide time and idle RAM: **not measured**. No window ran, so there are no screenshots. The only timings above are unsuccessful dependency resolution, not app/build performance.

Dev-loop friction: first restore is blocked by managed proxy connectivity. Successful compile cost is unknown. Effort estimate after unblock (planning judgment, not measured): 0.5–1 day for build/input gate including one bounded adapter; if it passes, 2–4 days for remaining editor/shell/carousel probes. Stop and reassess if input or wrapped interactive editor behavior requires a substantial rewrite.

